<title>BULGARIA: BALKAN COUNTRIES' RAILWAYS AGREE UNITED TARIFFS.</title>
<headline>BALKAN COUNTRIES' RAILWAYS AGREE UNITED TARIFFS.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Experts from seven Balkan countries on Thursday worked out united railway's tariffs to be confirmed by the countries' railway directors next month.</p>
<p>The tariffs' scheme, set up in the Bulgarian town of Plovdiv, will be in force after the meeting of the railway general directors from the Balkan countries in the Greek town of Tsessoloniki on November 20-21.</p>
<p>The countries involved are Bulgaria, Romania, Albania, Greece, Yugoslavia, Macedonia and Turkey, the state news agency BTA said.</p>
<p>Iran, Iraq and Syria are expected to join the united tariff agreement, BTA said.</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
